config SECURITY_CLOUDK
	bool "CloudOS kernel guard"
	depends on SECURITY
	default y
	help
	  CloudOS kernel guard. Exposes /proc/cloudk with the layer version
	  and the current hardening state, and enforces restrictive boot
	  defaults for kernel pointer exposure, dmesg access and oops
	  handling. Disable with the cloudk.guard=0 boot parameter.
